# PGlite writes a directory per database. Four of them were committed by accident
# in phase 2, when `scripts/migrate.mjs` still had a "run as a script" guard that
# fired inside the bundled CLI and read argv[2] — a command name — as a data
# directory. The guard is fixed; this is belt and braces for anything that lands
# a database at the repo root.
/*.pglite

# Throwaway probes at the repo root. They have to live here rather than in a
# temp directory, because `playwright` and `jszip` only resolve from inside the
# project — and one of them was committed in phase 11 before this rule existed.
/.*.mjs
